	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(20.0, 20.0, 560.0, 82.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">PRAKTIKUM 6 — Regression

TOP ROW: predicting a continuous target (house price).
BOTTOM ROW: predicting a binary target (default). The Nomogram is the widget
that makes logistic regression readable to a non-technical stakeholder.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(800.0, 140.0, 330.0, 250.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">WHAT TO DO
1. Test and Score (top): note RMSE, MAE and R2.
   Set 'Cross validation, 5 folds'.
2. Predicted-vs-actual scatter: is the spread even
   across the range, or does it fan out? That fan is
   heteroscedasticity (book section 6.4.1).
3. Logistic Regression: try Ridge (L2) with C=1,
   then Lasso (L1). Watch coefficients vanish.
4. NOMOGRAM: this is the payoff. Each feature is a
   line; the length of its bar is its influence.
   Drag the blue markers to score an applicant.
5. Confusion Matrix: which error does the model
   make more often? Is that the cheap one?</text>
	</annotations>
